dialogue.Colon.npc = Settler
dialogue.Colon.role = Ready to found a village
dialogue.Colon.hintFound = the village is founded right away
dialogue.Colon.hintFollow = follows you
dialogue.Colon.hintHome = goes back to the village
dialogue.Colon.aider = I'll help you: follow me.
dialogue.Colon.plusTard = Not now.
dialogue.Colon.accueilTexte = Our village has become a town, and some of us dream of new lands. Will you help me find where to found a village?
dialogue.Colon.enRoute = Let's go.
dialogue.Colon.suivreTexte = Thank you! Lead me wherever you like. Far from other villages, on our kind of land, and talk to me when you like the place.
dialogue.Colon.fonder = Let's found the village here.
dialogue.Colon.chercher = Let's keep looking.
dialogue.Colon.rentrer = Go back to the village, I'll come for you.
dialogue.Colon.iciTexte = I like this place: far enough from the others, good soil, no water. Shall we found the village here? My people are only waiting for my signal.
dialogue.Colon.tropPresPeupleTexte = Too close to another village of ours: each needs its own land and hunting grounds. Let's go further.
dialogue.Colon.tropPresAutreTexte = Another people lives close by. I won't settle on their doorstep.
dialogue.Colon.prevuTexte = Someone is already preparing a foundation close by. Let's look elsewhere.
dialogue.Colon.horsZoneTexte = These are not my people's lands. Take me back to our region.
dialogue.Colon.rivageTexte = Too close to the sea: storms would sweep our huts away. Let's go inland.
dialogue.Colon.eauTexte = There is too much water here: one does not build a village with wet feet.
dialogue.Colon.solTexte = This soil doesn't suit my people. We need ground of our own.
dialogue.Colon.reliefTexte = The ground is too rough for a square and houses. Let's find flatter land.
dialogue.Colon.examenTexte = I can't get a good look at the land from here. Let's move a little.
