dialogue.Kweebec_Marchand.role = merchant
dialogue.Kweebec_Marchand.honni = You? You made our trees weep sap. Leave before the guards see you.
dialogue.Kweebec_Marchand.etranger = I don't barter with strangers, traveller. Help the village, and my branch will open.
dialogue.Kweebec_Marchand.commentAider = How do I make myself known?
dialogue.Kweebec_Marchand.conseil = The crier, by the board, always has a small task for a stranger. One request fulfilled, then two, and you'll be tolerated.
dialogue.Kweebec_Marchand.voirDemandes = Show me the requests
dialogue.Kweebec_Marchand.accueil = Ah, the tolerated traveller! Seeds, sap, something to eat: here everything is paid in sap leaves.
dialogue.Kweebec_Marchand.ami = For a friend, I kept some winter berries and two lanterns that still sing.
dialogue.Kweebec_Marchand.hote = Our host! The elders let me open the reserve for you: the leaf crown would suit you.
dialogue.Kweebec_Marchand.troc = Let's see your wares
dialogue.Kweebec_Marchand.avance = And what you keep for friends?
dialogue.Kweebec_Marchand.reserve = Open the reserve for me
dialogue.Kweebec_Marchand.aurevoir = See you soon
dialogue.Kweebec_Crieur.honni = The village remembers what you did. If you want us to listen again, you'll have to earn it.
dialogue.Kweebec_Crieur.racheter = I want to make amends
